L3-R2 DRY RUNS of the prepared owner-decision scripts, each chain on a fresh copy of the registry.
Placeholder words 'dry run', date 2026-10-01. Nothing in the tree is written. The checked basis (fnd/l3plane cd8720a1,
CHECK-5) is filed, so the tree's rows are no longer held; the chains run on copies. Row L3-OD3's keep figures and
row L3-OD6's table come from FIXTURE files, except in the chain that reads the tree's filled table; row L3-OD4's band
is the basis's (none at U3's 6.0 A bracket); the push is a STAND-IN of 10 N for the owner's number, the pass line
kit-loads a stand-in for his sub-choice 1b, and 2 degrees the stand-in slope for a lid with no mechanical figure.
D-26: a target the studied candidate does not meet is recorded with its feasibility item; only requirements that
cannot both hold are refused. D-27: row L3-OD7 (M1's runtime) comes first; a chain reaching rows 1, 2, 4 or 6
starts with it answered 72-required, a STAND-IN for the owner's runtime answer.
The chains are examples, not recommendations.

